## 5. Predetermined change protocol for models (three tiers)

This protocol applies under [fill in: software validation procedure ID and clause] (section 2). Models change every few weeks and teams switch between them. This section is set **before** execution and is approved with this plan. It is an internal change-control mechanism, analogous in spirit to a predetermined change control plan; it is not a regulatory submission.

### 5.1 Tier 1: initial validation (once per tool and vendor)

- Full IQ, OQ and PQ of the guardrails as selected in section 6.
- MA-01, the model admission suite, on **every** model in the initial envelope (the "big first test"). For each family pattern in the envelope, the concrete model ids in use at validation time are listed and each one is run.
{{#policy_pinned}}
- Under the pinned policy the model in use is `{{pinned_model}}`: MA-01 and the full OQ run on it. Other envelope entries are not used by this tool unless they replace the pinned model through tier 3.
{{/policy_pinned}}
- Initial validation fixes the admission suite version and its acceptance criteria (section 5.4).
- Output: release decision in {{doc_id_07}}, with the approved envelope at release.

### 5.2 Tier 2: model admission (MA-01 only, per new model or model version)

{{#policy_envelope}}
Pre-authorised scope, one row per envelope entry (patterns use the kit's glob semantics, `*` and `?`; the vendor's own allow-list syntax is translated in {{doc_id_06}} section 12):

| Envelope entry | Pre-authorised pattern (glob) | Excluded ids |
|---|---|---|
{{#approved_models}}
| `{{.}}` | [fill in: e.g. dated or versioned releases of this entry; "none" = exact id only] | aliases such as `*-latest`, unversioned family names, preview or experimental ids, [fill in] |
{{/approved_models}}

- **Rule:** a new model id is Tier 2 only if it matches a pre-authorised pattern by glob and is not excluded; otherwise it is Tier 3 (section 5.3). Ids that the vendor can repoint to another model (for example `*-latest` or unversioned family names) are never admitted; only dated or versioned ids.
- **Eligibility (all yes, recorded in the admission record of {{doc_id_08}} section 7):** the id matches a pre-authorised pattern (which one); the tool version is inside the validated versions of {{doc_id_06}}; the IQ-03 re-capture equals the approved baseline (SHA-256); the release notes were screened (monitoring log reference) and contain no guardrail-relevant item. Any "no" routes the change to a change record (T3 or T7).
- **Detection:** vendor release or deprecation notice; a model id seen in telemetry, trailers, PR templates or in the `models_reported` field of the admission runner that has no admission record; checked [fill in: frequency, at least weekly with the monitoring routine of {{doc_id_08}}].
- **Activity:** re-run MA-01 with the frozen suite version, headless where the tool allows it, otherwise manually with the same tasks and criteria.
- **Pass:** the model is admitted; a short admission record (template in {{doc_id_08}}) is approved by the {{role_approver}} or [fill in: delegate] and is the revalidation record for this change; no further revalidation.
- **Fail:** the model is not admitted and is blocked where the tool can enforce it. If it was already in use, a deviation is raised and AI-assisted changes made with it since first use are assessed.
- **Enforcement:** the enforced allow-list contains admitted model ids only, never the pre-authorised pattern; an id is added after its admission record is approved.{{#is_claude_code}} For {{tool_name}}: managed `availableModels` with `availableModelsMatch` `"exact"` and `enforceAvailableModels` true, plus `deniedModels` for known unadmitted ids (both managed-only keys need a recent client version; record it in {{doc_id_06}}).{{/is_claude_code}} Where the tool cannot enforce this ([fill in: record which surfaces]), use before admission is expected, is detected by [fill in: telemetry or log check, frequency], and each occurrence is a deviation under T4 ({{doc_id_08}}) with review of the changes made. Such a deviation is pre-classified minor when MA-01 passes within [fill in: N] working days of first sighting and every change made with the model passed the human gate and CI in the meantime; otherwise major.
{{/policy_envelope}}
{{#policy_pinned}}
- Not available under the pinned policy: the AI output itself counts as a control or as evidence, so a change of the pinned model always follows tier 3 (confirmatory OQ subset plus MA-01, both passed before use).
- **Enforcement:** the enforced allow-list contains `{{pinned_model}}` only.{{#is_claude_code}} For {{tool_name}}: managed `availableModels` with `availableModelsMatch` `"exact"`, `enforceAvailableModels` true and `deniedModels` for known other ids.{{/is_claude_code}} Where the tool cannot enforce it ([fill in: record which surfaces]), every session records its model and any other model is a deviation under T4.
{{/policy_pinned}}

