## 8. Acceptance criteria fixed before execution

1. Every test in {{doc_id_05}} has an objective acceptance criterion, approved with the protocol before the first execution. Criteria, samples and expected results are not changed after execution starts. A needed change is a protocol amendment, approved before re-execution; earlier results are kept.
2. Where the tool computes or counts something, the expected result is computed independently, outside the tool, and recorded before the AI output is read.
3. Each test result is Pass, Fail or N/A with a written justification; an unresolved difference from the expected result is a Fail with a deviation.
4. Guardrail criteria (gates, permissions, protected paths, data rules) must be met in 100% of cases and runs.
5. The release decision is based on IQ, OQ and MA-01: all applicable IQ and OQ tests passed, or their deviations closed, or accepted open with risk assessment, restriction and target date as defined in {{doc_id_07}} section 7; MA-01 passed for {{#policy_envelope}}every model in the envelope at release{{/policy_envelope}}{{#policy_pinned}}the pinned model `{{pinned_model}}`{{/policy_pinned}}; residual risks accepted in {{doc_id_03}}. PQ-01 and PQ-02 verify after release that the validated configuration is effective: they start on the deployment date of the approved {{doc_id_06}} revision and are reported in a signed addendum to {{doc_id_07}} within [fill in: e.g. 8] weeks after release. Until that addendum is signed, the decision is "approved with conditions" (condition recorded in {{doc_id_07}} section 13). If PQ fails: suspend QMS-relevant use of the affected surface or context, raise a deviation, and assess every AI-assisted change merged in the PQ window.

## 9. Evidence rules

- Location: `evidence/{{tool_id}}/<TEST-ID>/` in [fill in: controlled evidence store linked to the eQMS]; the code-host part of the gate tests in `evidence/GEN/<TEST-ID>/` ({{doc_id_gates}}).
- File names: `evidence/{{tool_id}}/<TEST-ID>/<YYYYMMDD>-<short-description>.<ext>`, with `-r<n>` added for repeated runs, for example `evidence/{{tool_id}}/OQ-02/20260115-merge-refused-r1.json` (same convention as {{doc_id_05}}).
- Exploratory runs of the kit scripts before this plan and {{doc_id_05}} are approved go to `evidence/_exploratory/`. They only inform the plan and are not test evidence; the tests are re-run after approval.
- Prefer exports: API JSON, script output (JSON and Markdown with UTC timestamp and SHA-256), CLI transcripts, log extracts. Screenshots only where no export exists, with URL, date and account visible.
- Attribution: every kit script writes an `executed_by` block (operating-system user, host name, machine identifier, and the GitHub or tool login where available) and the operator name given with `--operator`.
- Integrity: the SHA-256 of every evidence file is written in the execution record in {{doc_id_05}} when the evidence is filed, and checked by the approver on a sample.
- Timestamps in UTC. Each record names the executor and the date and time of execution.
- Evidence about the AI tool is captured by scripts, platforms or people, never only by the AI tool's own account of what it did.
{{#code_github}}
- GitHub retention: the organisation audit log shows 180 days and Git events only 7 days. The Actions retention setting (default 90 days; private repositories up to 400) applies since 2026-10-01 also to checks, workflow runs and commit statuses, so required-check evidence on PRs is deleted after the retention period. Set it to the maximum your plan allows (`gh api -X PUT repos/{owner}/{repo}/actions/permissions/artifact-and-log-retention -F days=400` for private repositories), and export review records (`gh pr view <n> --json number,author,reviews,latestReviews,reviewDecision,mergedBy,mergedAt,mergeCommit,statusCheckRollup,commits`) and check runs when a PR is merged (`examples/github-workflow-evidence-export.yml`), and archive them in the evidence store.
{{/code_github}}
{{#code_gitlab}}
- GitLab: export `/projects/:id/merge_requests/:iid/approval_state` and the project approval settings for each sampled merge request, and archive the JSON.
{{/code_gitlab}}
- Retention: [fill in: retention period]{{#reg_iso13485}}; at least the lifetime of the device as defined by {{org_name}} and not less than two years from release (ISO 13485 clause 4.2.5), or longer where other regulations require, for example technical documentation periods{{/reg_iso13485}}.

